A busy morning can bring similar reports about different problems. Keep one
ticket per demonstrated cause within the same product. Merge only reports that
the evidence supports as duplicates.

## The rule

[Decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause) replaces the
[subject-only decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject), which remains
unchanged as a historical record.

1. Establish the product and read the report body. Find the tenant, its locale,
   the booking form version, and the channel used for this report.
2. Compare the demonstrated mechanism with an existing issue. In the exported
   `sched-prod` date reports, use `tenantOf`, `causeOf`, and `sameCause` from
   `src/lib/kb`, not the browser locale or intake tag.
3. Merge only when the cause is known and matches within the same product.
   Count each report ID once, even if the export repeats it.
4. If the cause differs, keep a separate issue. If context is missing or the
   body contradicts the classification, preserve the uncertainty and investigate.

<Callout>
Matching subjects can hide different causes. Different subjects can describe the
same cause. An unknown tenant is not proof of duplication.
</Callout>

## Try it

<DedupeExplorer />

## When you are unsure

Do not merge on a subject match alone. Ask for the missing context and preserve
the original report. The live example rejects an unknown cause even when both
subjects match.

The [signed review of #4471](/kb/incidents/4471-split) links the separate parser
and form-hint issues and retains the desk's unexplained one-day observations.
